        "label": "Read a few fields of many records of one kind",
        "job": "Read named top-level fields of many records of one kind from their attribute facts without assembling any record: the fields of given ids, the records after a value, the newest record per group, and the ids whose field holds a value",
        "description": "Lays out the records given in records ([{ id, type, value }]) in an in-memory SQLite database (node:sqlite) with the EEAF store's own entity, entity_types, type_properties and attribute_fact tables (their CREATE statements read from do-work/eeaf-sqlite-store.mjs as text), each record's top-level scalars and lists of scalars as attribute facts under the store's ids (type:<type>, prop:<type>:<field>, the value as JSON). A field holding an object or a list of objects is not laid out (in the store it lives on child subjects, which a field read never answers) and is named in left_out. Then answers each of reads (each under its name, its place in the list when left out, with count: how many records or ids it found) through eeafFieldReads (do-work/eeaf-field-reads.mjs): fieldsOf { type, ids, fields } (an id not held as that type is left out), after { type, field, after, fields?, limit?, after_id? } (oldest first, compared as kept JSON text, so ISO times sort), newestPerGroup { type, group, order, fields? } and idsWhere { type, field, value, limit? }. Reads nothing but the input, writes no file, sends nothing; the database is gone when the run ends. Refuses a record without an id or type, an id with a slash, a value that is not an object, the same id twice, an unknown op, a read missing what its op needs and two reads with the same name. The old store keeps a person's records on their own device, logs every change and assembles whole records (eeafStore); this run does none of that: eeaf-sqlite-store.mjs imports parts/record-log/do-work/record-log-store.mjs, which the Workshop does not have, so it is packed only as the text its tables are read from.",
